CM_ "GWM Haval H6 PHEV19 2026 (MK4). Minimal working set: the signals CarState
reads plus the STEER_CMD frame CarController writes. Bus assignment matters -
STEER_CMD (299), LATERAL_STATE (573) and ACC (683) are transmitted by the
forward camera and are only visible on the camera bus once the harness relay
opens; everything else is on the main car bus.";

CM_ SG_ 161 STEERING_ANGLE "Absolute wheel angle magnitude, 0.1 deg. Sign is in
STEERING_DIRECTION (1 = right/CW, 0 = left/CCW), applied in carstate. This is
the real angle - message 327 is DRIVER TORQUE, not angle.";
CM_ SG_ 161 STEERING_RATE "Wheel angle rate magnitude; sign is in RATE_DIRECTION
(non-zero = right/CW), applied in carstate.";
CM_ SG_ 299 STEER_REQUEST "Commanded absolute wheel angle. raw = (deg+779.6)*10,
zero at raw 7796. The -779.6 offset is the EPS command-to-wheel transfer, tuned
so the wheel settles on the commanded angle.";
CM_ SG_ 299 CRC_STEER "byte16 = CRC-8 (poly 0x1D, init 0x05) over bytes 17-23.
Recompute on every send. Verified 3002/3002 on an OEM-engaged segment and
2999/2999 on an openpilot-engaged segment.";
CM_ SG_ 299 CRC_COUNTER "byte8 = CRC-8 (poly 0x1D, init 0xD1) over bytes 9-15,
which include COUNTER_1. Recompute whenever COUNTER_1 changes. Same verification
as CRC_STEER.";
CM_ SG_ 299 COUNTER_1 "byte15 low nibble. ALWAYS equal to COUNTER_2 in every
captured frame (3002/3002 and 2999/2999) - the EPS sees a single logical counter
written into two places, each covered by its own CRC. Send both, and increment
from the camera's value.";
CM_ SG_ 299 COUNTER_2 "byte23 low nibble. See COUNTER_1.";
CM_ SG_ 299 EPS_LKAS_ANGLE_ENABLE "byte21: 0x3f = EPS executes STEER_REQUEST,
0x1f = passive/ignore. Set 0x3f only while actively steering; mirror the
camera's value otherwise.";
CM_ SG_ 299 EPS_LKAS_ANGLE_CFG "byte22: 0xe5 active, 0x81 passive.";
CM_ SG_ 327 DRIVER_TORQUE "Driver-applied steering torque, signed. For
override/hands-on detection, NOT vehicle angle.";
CM_ SG_ 327 EPS_STEER_REQUESTED "1 = EPS is executing the camera/openpilot angle,
2 = driver override. NOT a fault indicator - it reads 2 for long stretches of
healthy driving - so it is exposed for diagnostics only and is not wired to any
CarState fault field.";
CM_ SG_ 327 EPS_FAULT_PERMANENT "Toggles 0/1 during normal operation on this
platform, so it is NOT usable as steerFaultPermanent.";
CM_ SG_ 573 LKAS_STATE "5 = lane centering active.";
CM_ SG_ 683 CRUISE_ENGAGED "byte47 bit4. The engagement flag: high through every
labelled ACC and ICC run of the 2026-08-18 differential drive and low outside
them. This is what carstate and the panda safety mode both read, so the two
gates cannot disagree.";
CM_ SG_ 683 CRUISE_STATE "3 = engaged (5 is a brief ICC-engage transient), 1/2 =
not engaged. Corroborates CRUISE_ENGAGED on the same drive; kept for diagnostics.";

VAL_ 545 GEAR_REAL 0 "P" 1 "D" 2 "N" 3 "R" ;
VAL_ 573 LKAS_STATE 5 "active" 2 "hands_on_required" 3 "drift_left" 4 "drift_right" ;
VAL_ 683 CRUISE_STATE 1 "inactive" 2 "available" 3 "engaged" 5 "engaging_icc" ;

CM_ SG_ 199 GEAR_STALK_POSITION "Enumerated stalk position, always a multiple of 15. Measured over 59494 frames: 1 rest, 3 soft UP, 4 hard UP, 5 soft DOWN, 6 hard DOWN. The stock ACC engages on HARD down - every stock engagement in our captures was preceded by one - and ignores SOFT down entirely, which appeared 9 times and never once with cruise engaged. Soft down is therefore usable as openpilot's own engage gesture without ever starting the stock ACC.";
CM_ SG_ 199 STALK_DOWN "Set for both soft and hard down. Pair with STALK_FURTHER to tell them apart.";
CM_ SG_ 199 STALK_FURTHER "The hard detent. DOWN+FURTHER is the stock ACC gesture; DOWN alone is ours.";
CM_ SG_ 199 CRC "crc8 over bytes 1..7, poly 0x1D, init 0xC1. Verified 4000/4000.";
VAL_ 199 GEAR_STALK_POSITION 15 "rest" 45 "soft_up" 60 "hard_up" 75 "soft_down" 90 "hard_down" ;
